##Problem:
After loading olist_order_reviews_dataset.csv into bronze.order_reviews_data, the table had 99,223 rows. 
The source file has 99,224 rows (counted in Excel, excluding header). One row was missing, with no error message.
=======================================================================================================================

=======================================================================================================================
##Root cause (probable):
The CSV is UTF-8 and contains Portuguese characters. 
The load did not specify the code page, and the comment columns were VARCHAR. Text was misread (e.g. “não” appeared as “n+úo”) and one row was lost.
=======================================================================================================================

=======================================================================================================================
##Fix:
BULK INSERT now uses CODEPAGE = '65001' (UTF-8).
review_comment_title and review_comment_message changed to NVARCHAR.
Reloaded with bronze.load_bronze.
=======================================================================================================================

##Verification:
Row count now 99,224, which matches the source. Accents display correctly.

##How to prevent it:
After every file load, compare the row count with the source file before moving on.
=======================================================================================================================

=======================================================================================================================
WITH (
    FORMAT     = 'CSV',
    FIRSTROW   = 2,
    FIELDQUOTE = '"',
    CODEPAGE   = '65001',
    TABLOCK
);

ALTER TABLE bronze.order_reviews_data ALTER COLUMN review_comment_title   NVARCHAR(200);
ALTER TABLE bronze.order_reviews_data ALTER COLUMN review_comment_message NVARCHAR(MAX);
